# Course: Qauntitative Reasoning

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',         'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl'
);

@list1 = ('airline', 'bus station', 'train station');
@list2 = ('flight',  'bus',         'train');
$ind   = random(0,   2   );
$num   = random(25,  150);
$line = Compute(random(100,250). "x + " . random(100,250))->reduce; 


BEGIN_PGML

An [$list1[$ind]] has determined that the relationship between the number of passengers on a [$list2[$ind]] and the total
weight of luggage stored in the baggage compartment can be estimated by the least squares 
regression equation [` y = [$line] `]. Predict the weight of luggage for a flight with [$num] passengers.

Answer: [_]{$line->eval(x => $num)}{20} pounds

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
This is found by subsitutine [`x= [$num]`] into the line [`y=[$line]`] or [` [$line->eval(x => $num)]`] pounds.
END_PGML_SOLUTION


ENDDOCUMENT();      